  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Daily rain chances with seasonable temperatures\nthis weekend and into early next week.\n\nA broad upper-level trough will begin to form over the Ohio River \nValley over the weekend. As this trough tracks east, cloud cover & \nprecipitation chances will begin to increase, particularly between \nSaturday evening and Sunday as the low tracks offshore and towards \nthe northeast. Severe probabilities look low at this time, with a \npretty weak wind field aloft. Nonetheless, weekend showers are \npossible with this system should the synoptic setup continue to \ntrend toward development over the Midwest.\n\nDespite possible weekend showers, temperatures on Sunday through \nTuesday remain seasonable for late July with highs hovering in the \nupper 80s east of the Blue Ridge and upper 70s west of the Blue \nRidge. Overnight lows remain consistently in the low 70s (east \nof BR) and mid 60s (west of BR). Best chances for showers remain\non Sunday, coinciding with the upper-level low mentioned \npreviously, but chances of showers remain in the 10-20% into \nearly next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Dry conditions through the end of the week. \n\nIn the wake of a strong frontal system, surface high pressure\nbuilds over the mid-atlantic with primarily dry conditions and\nseasonable temperatures expected. An isolated rain shower or\nperhaps a thunderstorm cannot be ruled out each afternoon as\ndaytime heating leads to slightly increased instability.\nHowever, conditions across the forecast area are expected to be\ndry with rain chances remaining low. \n\nHighs will gradually increase each day with temperatures staying\nin the 70s to upper 80s. On Friday, some locations in the\nsouthern portions of the region may reach 90 degrees.",
